{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"atrophied-exact-indianabat","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Discovered from\n\nrebar-debug on bug `smart-disloyal-naga` (8386-a512-4815-4e6b), via an independent\nwrite-safety audit of the materialized ticket-store entry. Not a root cause of 8386; a\nseparate defect found while proving that one.\n\n## Problem\n\n`<store>/tickets-<sha>/` is documented and treated as an **immutable, content-addressed**\nentry (ADR 0005 D2). It is not. Every `show_ticket` read through the pinned root writes a\nderived reducer cache **inside the entry**:\n\n`reducer/_api.py:221` -> `write_cache(cache_path, ...)` with\n`cache_path = os.path.join(ticket_dir, \".cache.json\")` (`reducer/_cache.py:196`, published at\n`:146` via `atomic_write`). A second site, `reducer/_processors.py:58`, writes the same file on\nthe corrupt-CREATE replay path.\n\n**Measured on this host:** one live entry\n(`tickets-00b00a6ee3e2b6c0ebb667c044eb303ccf2ba3e3`) holds **4,844 `.cache.json` files**, every\none with an mtime newer than the entry directory itself — i.e. created by reads after\nmaterialization, not by `checkout-index`. They are gitignored on the tickets branch, so they are\nabsent from the committed tree and are purely post-build artifacts.\n\n## Why it matters\n\n1. **The immutability premise is false**, and other code is entitled to rely on it. Bug 8386's\n   fix now hardlinks unchanged blobs between adjacent entries; it is safe only because\n   `atomic_write` publishes by `os.replace` (`_store/fsutil.py:96`) rather than writing in\n   place. That is an incidental property of one line, not an enforced invariant. If that line\n   ever becomes a plain `open(path, \"w\")`, every entry sharing the inode is silently corrupted.\n2. **It already breaks the reverify pass.** `janitor.reverify_entry` (`janitor.py:249-277`)\n   records a TOFU digest over the entry's contents at first sight. Reads keep adding\n   `.cache.json` files afterwards, so a baseline taken before the first read makes the entry\n   look **corrupt** on the next pass and evicts it. Opt-in today (`reverify_seconds > 0`), which\n   is the only reason this has not bitten.\n3. It inflates the store, which is the parent bug's whole subject: ~4.8k extra files per entry.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Reading a ticket through a pinned snapshot root does not write into the snapshot entry\n      (e.g. the reducer cache is disabled, or redirected outside the entry, when the tracker\n      root is a snapshot).\n- [ ] A test observes the write RED (a materialized entry's file set changes after a read) and\n      GREEN after the fix.\n- [ ] The rename-over contract in `_store/fsutil.py` is pinned by a test, or the entry is made\n      genuinely read-only, so a future in-place write cannot silently corrupt shared inodes.\n- [ ] ADR 0005's immutability claim is either enforced or amended to describe reality.","id":"5c27-7926-835f-4563","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Snapshot entries are not immutable: every ticket read writes .cache.json inside them"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787293854709370001,"uuid":"7a7bc711-a378-4c05-92e7-78951ef4e4fd"}